  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On the Promenade de la Mer in Menton, Le Festival Plage serves Italian cuisine and fresh seafood in a family-friendly waterfront setting. Sunny terrace, relaxed atmosphere: it's a convenient address for lunch or dinner facing the sea, at the eastern tip of the French Riviera.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>On booking platforms, it's possible to note whether you're coming with a dog, and several customer reviews mention a positive welcome for dogs on the terrace. This information does not come from an official statement by the restaurant about its own dog policy: it's best to confirm by phone before coming, especially in high season when the terrace fills up fast. Hours: Monday to Saturday 9am to 11pm, Sunday 9am to 6:30pm.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the Garavan dog beach, the only beach in Menton where dogs are allowed, is at the other end of town — plan for a trip if you want to combine a swim and a meal with your dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Menton's old town and its colourful lanes are a few minutes' walk away, as are the Jardins Biovès that run through the town centre.</p>
    </div>

